// D1589 — the value is a `??` READ of an A-infer-null hole taken BEFORE the assignment that
// fills it. `let h = null` binds `mkNullableTy(-1)`; the read types against a `nInner` that is
// still `-1`, so `nonNullTy` hands back the NULLABLE ITSELF and the bank aliases the very
// arena node the later `h = 5` mutates in place. After the fill every emit-side consumer
// reads `i32 | null` for an expression `emitCoalesce` lowers UNBOXED — a box-shaped
// destination taking a raw i32, `vl check` rc 0, at every position the read is delivered to.
//
// THE SETUP IS THE WHOLE DEFECT and the delivery is what it infects: the hole, the read, and
// the fill are three statements in the delivery's own scope, so each position exercises the
// storage class the hole actually has there (a function local, a start-fn local, a module
// global). `__fill` is a global so the fill is a real branch rather than a folded one.
//
// The PROOF discriminates on the read's VALUE, so a cell that delivered the box where an i32
// was owed refuses or prints the wrong word rather than passing.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
let __fill = true
// @@SETUP@@
let __h = null
const __r = __h ?? 0
if __fill { __h = 5 }
// @@VALUE@@
__r
// @@TYPE@@
i32
// @@TEST@@
v == 0
// @@HIT@@
print("zero")
// @@MISS@@
print("other")
// @@WANT@@
zero
